IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate

-- WHICH TEXT ANSWERS ON WHICH DATE.
-- Build 98 of `main` has no EVAL UNDER RULES EFFECTIVE AT, so each vintage is an explicit date window,
-- and a rule that depends on the text takes the date as an input and answers NOTHING outside the window.
-- A window says only: "the text deposited is the text in force on these dates, as far as the deposit shows".
-- It never says what the law was before the deposited text's own in-force date: no past text of the Act
-- or of any instrument was obtained (see NOTES.md, "Editions encoded and where each text could not be had").

§ `The last day the sources were checked`

-- ASSUMED, NOT RULED: 4 November 2026. The Act's consolidation was retrieved on 1 October 2026 (BA1994.meta.json), the lawplain instruments on 3 November 2026 and the Gazette texts on 3 and 4 November 2026.
-- On 4 November 2026 the orchestrating session searched the e-Gazette index for 'Broadcasting Act' (year 2026: 22 results; 'Broadcasting Act amendment', 2025 to 2026: 7 results; first page of each) and read the three results that name the Act: Act 13 of 2026 (it amends the Info-communications Media Development Authority Act 2016 and the Telecommunications Act 1999, and refers to the Broadcasting Act's licences under sections 8 and 21 without amending any provision of it; first published 5 June 2026, in operation on a date to be appointed by notification, which was not found), the Digital Infrastructure Bill (Bill 20/2026, first published 8 September 2026; a Bill, not law; it names the Broadcasting Act once, in its explanatory statement; https://assets.egazette.gov.sg/2026/Legislative%20Supplements/Bills%20Supplement/26bills20.pdf, sha256 e74a98b41a04a54bb1a97ce9cd25dd7966f42f3ff087c216286528bc05a55408), and S 700/2026 (Info-communications Media Development Authority (Regulated Persons) Notification 2026, in operation 2 October 2026, made under the IMDA Act; https://assets.egazette.gov.sg/2026/Legislative%20Supplements/Subsidiary%20Legislation%20Supplement/26sls700.pdf, sha256 70f1358cb250167422af6f10cbc5ad5cde53ad8abe4dee2f9acff17be8c04bf5).
-- The other results are titles under other Acts and were not read.
-- None of the three amends a provision of the Broadcasting Act.
-- That is what a first-page index search and three readings show; it is not a finding that nothing exists.
-- Every window below, and the version tables of sgba-versions.l4, stop on this day: a reading or conduct day after it answers NOTHING because no later source was seen, and a day up to it is answered from the latest text deposited.
-- To revert to the earlier cutoff, change the one line below to `Date 1 10 2026` (the consolidation's retrieval day); the tests that name a reading day of 2 October to 4 November 2026 and expect an answer would then fail and are set back by hand.
`the day the sources were last checked` MEANS Date 4 11 2026

§ `The Act`

-- The deposited text of the Act is the informal consolidation "version in force from 25/9/2024"
-- (BA1994.txt:15) retrieved on 2026-10-01 (BA1994.meta.json: "Current version as at 01 Oct 2026"). Its window runs to the day the sources were last checked (assumed, not ruled).
GIVEN d IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the deposited text of the Act is the text in force on` MEANS
    d AT LEAST (Date 25 9 2024) AND d AT MOST `the day the sources were last checked`

§ `The instruments`

-- Each instrument is the text lawplain served on 2026-11-03 (one version only). The window opens on the date
-- the text itself gives for its coming into operation (the revised-edition date or the latest amendment it
-- shows) and closes on the day the sources were last checked (4 November 2026, assumed, not ruled), the day the brief calls "today" being 3 November 2026.
-- Whether an instrument was amended or revoked after the version served is not shown by the text served.

GIVEN d IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the TVRO System Regulations as deposited are the text in force on` MEANS
    d AT LEAST (Date 29 2 2004) AND d AT MOST `the day the sources were last checked`

